#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# differences

#% text
# `differences(xs)` gives the successive differences `[x2 - x1, x3 - x2, ...]` of the list `xs`.

#% text
# `differences(xs, n)` gives the n-th differences.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The result has one element fewer than `xs` (n fewer for the n-th differences).

#% item
# On a long list of machine reals the differences are computed directly on the numbers.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
differences([1, 4, 9, 16, 25])
#% output
#= [3, 5, 7, 9]

#% cell
differences([1, 4, 9, 16, 25], 2)
#% output
#= [2, 2, 2]

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Symbolic elements:

#% cell
differences([a, b, c])
#% output
#= [b - a, c - b]

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# `accumulate` of the differences gives the elements less the first one:

#% cell
xs = [3, 1, 4, 1, 5]
accumulate(differences(xs)) == rest(xs) - first(xs)
#% output
#= true

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `accumulate`, `fold_list`, `total`
